Ticket **#4471** merged **412** unique date reports and was marked known as one parser bug.
The cause table below is built from the same export the desk uses. It shows **two** causes
inside that merge. Each needs its own engineering ticket.

<Callout>
#4471 is not one issue. Split it before you queue a single fix.
</Callout>

## What #4471 really holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Tickets filed

| cause | reports | desk ticket |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| `parser` | 379 | [ccswift/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows#1](https://github.com/ccswift/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) |
| `hint` | 33 | [ccswift/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows#2](https://github.com/ccswift/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) |

- **parser** — shared parser reads dates month-first; day-first tenants flip month and day.
- **hint** — booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the field; day-first tenants type the hint,
  and the form reads it their way. Same symptom, different bug.

Intake tags and subject-line dedupe both treat these as one pile. The tenant + form path in
`causeOf` is what separates them.

## Why this page

Decision [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone. That was right
for speed and wrong for #4471: twelve subjects, two causes. Keep the merge rule for triage;
re-read with `CauseTable` before you mark a big ticket known.

